  "code": "INELIG",
  "loc": "1. Introduction, p. 3",
  "quote": "designing a decentralized mechanism that consists of message spaces, an allocation rule",
  "note": "Implementation-theory / mechanism-design paper. A central planner elicits agents' information about the state through message spaces, quadratic-scoring-rule payments and fines. The main object is the design of mechanisms with monetary transfers for implementing SCFs in BNE, not a voting procedure aggregating voters' inputs. A majority rule appears only as one component of the constructed mechanism (Section 4.2.1)."
